<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna `signedness`: an integer local whose every comparison is signed is
    declared unsigned, and the cast machinery writes the signedness back at each
    use.

    Datatype::type_order ranks SUB_UINT_PLAIN (16) ahead of SUB_INT_PLAIN (17),
    so in get_local_type's "keep the most specific" fold one uint vote outranks
    every int vote on the same Varnode, and nothing downstream re-decides.  On
    -O2 x86-64 those uint votes are structural: a strength-reduced loop bound is
    masked (INT_AND, which votes TYPE_UINT on both operands) even when every
    comparison on it is signed.

    Bytes at 0x1000, the reduced shape (three parameters so the masked value is
    declared rather than inlined at each use):

        1000  89 f8                 MOV  EAX,EDI
        1002  01 f0                 ADD  EAX,ESI
        1004  25 f8 ff ff 7f        AND  EAX,0x7ffffff8   ; the TYPE_UINT vote
        1009  39 c2                 CMP  EDX,EAX
        100b  7d 06                 JGE  0x1013           ; signed
        100d  01 c2                 ADD  EDX,EAX
        100f  39 c2                 CMP  EDX,EAX
        1011  7c fa                 JL   0x100d           ; signed
        1013  89 d0                 MOV  EAX,EDX
        1015  c3                    RET

    Stage: P9 emission, sub-stage "naming-policy" (the declaration seam, next
    to kuna_declhightype).  P0 assertion: `option signedness
    upstream|auto|prefer-signed|prefer-unsigned`.

    Pass 1 (default `upstream`) reproduces it: `uint4 v1;` declared, and the two
    signed comparisons carry a `(int4)` cast (asserts #1 and #2).
    Pass 2 (`option signedness auto`) declares `int4 v1;` (every
    signedness-sensitive reader of v1 demands signed and none demands unsigned)
    and the cast, now a no-op against that declaration, is dropped (asserts #3
    and #4).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000">
89f801f025f8ffff7f39c27d0601c239c27cfa89d0c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="f"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option signedness upstream</com>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option signedness auto</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="signedness #1: the masked loop bound is declared unsigned under the default (bug reproduces, once)" min="1" max="1">^  uint4 v1; // eax$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="signedness #2: and every signed comparison on it carries a cast back to int4 (bug reproduces, once)" min="1" max="1">a2 &lt; \(int4\)v1</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="signedness #3: option signedness auto declares it at the signedness its operations demand (fix, once)" min="1" max="1">^  int4 v1; // eax$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="signedness #4: and the cast the declaration makes a no-op is dropped (fix, once)" min="1" max="1">a2 &lt; v1;</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
